<div class="marketing-homepage">
  <section id="planner" class="marketing-section planner-hero halo-section">
    <div class="hero-copy reveal-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span>Web planner · No account required</p>
      <h1>Plan the <em>whole meeting</em>.<br />Not just the start.</h1>
      <p class="hero-supporting">Compare the complete meeting interval across local Working, Border and Sleep hours.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/planner">Open Planner</a>
        <p>Free. No account required. <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a class="text-link" href="/download">RealTimeZones Desktop →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="product-window planner-window reveal-product">
      <figcaption class="window-bar">
        <span class="window-address"><i></i><i></i><i></i><b>realtimezones.com/planner</b></span>
        <span><strong><span class="desktop-only">60-minute meeting</span><span class="mobile-only">60 min</span></strong><span class="desktop-only"> · 3 local time zones</span></span>
      </figcaption>
      <div class="temporal-grid planner-proof-padding">
        <div class="planner-proof-crop">
          <picture>
            <source media="(max-width: 767px)" srcset="/marketing/planner-mobile-hero-60-1500.png 1x, /marketing/planner-mobile-hero-60-1500@3x.png 3x" />
            <img src="/marketing/planner-desktop-hero-60-1500.png" width="1400" height="816" alt="RealTimeZones planner comparing a 60-minute meeting across three local time zones" />
          </picture>
        </div>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="duration" class="marketing-section duration-section">
    <div class="section-heading centered-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span>Duration matters · Friday, Sep 18, 2026</p>
      <h2>Same start.<br />A <em>longer meeting</em> changes the local impact.</h2>
      <p>The same start time can produce a different local exposure mix as the meeting gets longer.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="duration-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Meeting duration comparison">
      <button id="duration-tab-60" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="duration-panel-60" data-duration-tab>60 min</button>
      <button id="duration-tab-90" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="duration-panel-90" tabindex="-1" data-duration-tab>90 min</button>
    </div>

    <div class="duration-comparison">
      <article id="duration-panel-60" class="duration-card is-active" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="duration-tab-60" data-duration-panel>
        <div class="mini-window-bar"><span>realtimezones.com/planner</span><strong>60 min</strong></div>
        <picture>
          <source media="(max-width: 767px)" srcset="/marketing/planner-mobile-duration-60-1500.png 1x, /marketing/planner-mobile-duration-60-1500@3x.png 3x" />
          <img src="/marketing/planner-desktop-duration-60-1500.png" width="620" height="234" alt="60-minute planner state" loading="lazy" />
        </picture>
        <div class="duration-detail">
          <p class="mono-label">Local impact breakdown <span>15:00–16:00</span></p>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Your Location</dt><dd>15:00–16:00 · Working</dd></div>
            <div><dt>London</dt><dd>10:30–11:30 · Working</dd></div>
            <div><dt>New York</dt><dd>05:30–06:30 · 30m Sleep + 30m Border</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="duration-delta" aria-hidden="true"><span>→</span><small>+30 min</small></div>

      <article id="duration-panel-90" class="duration-card" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="duration-tab-90" data-duration-panel>
        <div class="mini-window-bar"><span>realtimezones.com/planner</span><strong>90 min</strong></div>
        <picture>
          <source media="(max-width: 767px)" srcset="/marketing/planner-mobile-duration-90-1500.png 1x, /marketing/planner-mobile-duration-90-1500@3x.png 3x" />
          <img src="/marketing/planner-desktop-duration-90-1500.png" width="620" height="234" alt="90-minute planner state" loading="lazy" />
        </picture>
        <div class="duration-detail">
          <p class="mono-label">Local impact breakdown <span>15:00–16:30</span></p>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Your Location</dt><dd>15:00–16:30 · Working</dd></div>
            <div><dt>London</dt><dd>10:30–12:00 · Working</dd></div>
            <div class="changed"><dt>New York</dt><dd>05:30–07:00 · 30m Sleep + 60m Border</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <aside class="change-summary">
      <strong>What changed</strong>
      <p>Extending the meeting by 30 minutes adds another 30 minutes inside New York’s Border period.</p>
      <span>60m: 30m Sleep + 30m Border → 90m: 30m Sleep + 60m Border</span>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section id="capabilities" class="marketing-section split-section capabilities-section">
    <div class="section-heading sticky-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span>Built for the whole decision</p>
      <h2>See the full impact <em>before you send</em> the invite.</h2>
      <p>RealTimeZones compares the complete meeting interval in every selected city, helping you choose a time that works before you share or export the plan.</p>
      <ul class="scope-list">
        <li>Up to 50 cities in locally stored or shared planner state</li>
        <li>Meeting durations from 15 minutes to 12 hours</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <ol class="feature-ledger">
      <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Complete interval evaluation</h3><p>The full meeting interval is evaluated—not only its start time.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Duration-aware recommendations</h3><p>Suggested times respond to the selected duration and local hours in every selected city.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Multi-city comparison</h3><p>Compare the same interval across your selected cities in one aligned timeline.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>04</span><div><h3>Working-hour context</h3><p>Working, Border and Sleep labels make local impact visible without reducing the result to a score.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>05</span><div><h3>Shareable planner state</h3><p>Copy a planner URL that preserves the selected cities, date, start time, duration and time format.</p><small>Example · 15:00 start · 60 min<br />realtimezones.com/planner?cities=London%2CNew%20York&amp;focus=15&amp;date=2026-09-18&amp;duration=60&amp;format=24h</small></div></li>
      <li><span>06</span><div><h3>Calendar export</h3><p>Open a pre-filled Google Calendar or Outlook event, or download an ICS file for Apple Calendar and compatible calendar apps.</p><small>Google Calendar · Outlook · Apple Calendar · ICS File</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy" class="marketing-section privacy-section">
    <div class="section-heading centered-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span>Local by default</p>
      <h2>Plan <em>without an account</em>.</h2>
      <p>Planner state is stored in your browser. Share links contain the meeting state you choose, and external calendar destinations open only after an explicit action.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="trust-grid">
      <li>Local browser storage</li>
      <li>No account required</li>
      <li>Shareable planner URLs</li>
      <li>Offline-capable after loading</li>
      <li>Explicit external calendar actions</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

